# Side buffer and background expansion for ALEX-OL (paper Section 5), plus fixes to
# released ALEX-OL that every configuration, including the baseline, is built with.
#
# Applies after alexol-stagger.patch and alexol-contention-stats.patch, in alexol/src:
#   patch -p0 -d alexol/src -i alexol-sidebuf.patch
#
# Design, off by default, so an unflagged run behaves as ALEX-OL with the fixes below:
#   sidebuf::enabled()  inserts and lookups proceed during a rebuild via a sealed side buffer
#   bgexp::enabled()    inserts past a soft threshold enqueue the node for background threads
# The bench driver sets them with the `side`, `bg`, `bgsoft=` and `bgthreads=` flags.
#
# Fixes to released ALEX-OL:
#   - root expansion did not update existing children's local depth, so a later rebuild of
#     such a child computed too many parent slots and overwrote its siblings, losing their
#     subtrees (millions of keys under a small bulk load, also single-threaded);
#   - root expansion mutated the live root in place (model shifted before the child array
#     was swapped, array published before its new slots were filled) and freed the old
#     array under lock-free readers; it now builds the new root privately, publishes it
#     with one store, holds the root's and the outermost data node's locks, and retires
#     rather than frees the old array;
#   - a rebuild copied the leaf, including its depth, before locking the parent, so a root
#     expansion in between left the replacement with a stale depth; it now takes the depth
#     after the parent lock;
#   - a lookup that misses checks the adjacent leaves, because a split and a lookup can
#     disagree on which side of a boundary a 64-bit key falls (observed on SOSD osm).
#
# Also refactors the structural-modification body of Alex::insert into run_smo() unchanged,
# so the background threads run the same code, and extends the contention counters with
# restart attribution and slow-insert classification (enabled by `lockstats`).
