+// Side buffer. While a node is being rebuilt, its holder keeps the lock for the whole
+// copy, and every insert or lookup that reaches the node restarts until the copy ends.
+// With the side buffer, the holder publishes a small buffer before it starts copying.
+// Inserts that find the node locked append to the buffer instead of restarting, and
+// lookups read the old node, which the rebuild only reads, plus the buffer. The holder
+// seals the buffer after copying, applies its entries to the new node, and publishes the
+// new node as before. Inserts that arrive after sealing restart as they do today; that
+// window covers only the apply and the parent update, not the copy.
+namespace sidebuf {
+inline bool &enabled() { static bool e = false; return e; }
+constexpr int kCap = 1024;
+}  // namespace sidebuf
